Microsoft Learn: Introduction to Azure Backup

Platform: Microsoft Learn
Module: Introduction to Azure Backup
Track: AZ-104 Microsoft Azure Administrator
Difficulty: Beginner
Date: 2026

Objective

Learn what Azure Backup is, how it protects Azure and on-premises workloads, and when organizations should use Azure Backup to support business continuity and disaster recovery.

This module focused on understanding Azure Backup as a cloud-native backup solution, how backup and recovery operations work, and how Azure Administrators can use backup services to protect critical business data and infrastructure.

Step 1: Understanding Azure Backup

The module introduced Azure Backup as Microsoft's cloud-based backup and recovery service.

Azure Backup helps organizations protect:

Azure Virtual Machines
Azure Files
SQL Server databases
Azure workloads
On-premises servers
On-premises virtual machines
Key benefits:
Centralized backup management
Long-term retention
Secure storage
Automated backups
Disaster recovery support
Example:
Azure Virtual Machine
         ↓
Azure Backup
         ↓
Recovery Services Vault

The module emphasized that backup is a critical component of business continuity planning.

Step 2: Why Organizations Need Backups

The training covered common situations where backups are required.

Common risks:
Accidental deletion
Data corruption
Hardware failures
Malware attacks
Ransomware
Application failures
Human error
Administrative goals:
Recover lost data
Minimize downtime
Meet compliance requirements
Support disaster recovery
Key lesson learned:

High availability does not replace backups.

Even highly available systems still require backup protection.

Step 3: Understanding Recovery Services Vault

A major focus of the module was the Recovery Services Vault.

The Recovery Services Vault is the central management component for Azure Backup.

Functions:
Stores backup metadata
Maintains recovery points
Applies backup policies
Manages retention settings
Example:
Recovery Services Vault

├── VM Backups
├── SQL Backups
├── File Share Backups
└── Recovery Points
Benefits:
Centralized management
Secure backup storage
Simplified administration

The module emphasized that most Azure Backup deployments begin with a Recovery Services Vault.

